The minimum counter example $G$ satisfies the following properties,
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] $\forall u,v \in N_{G}(p)$, $(u,v) \notin E(G)$.
\item[(b)] $\forall z_i \in N_{G}(p)-\{q,p'\}$ and $\forall v \in N_{G}(p)$, we have $(v,z'_i) \notin E(G)$.
\end{enumerate}
\end{lem}

This Lemma is not explicitly used in the proof, but we believe that this information will help the reader to visualize the situation better.

~~~~~~

In view of $Lemma$ \ref{lem:lem17} let $e_1$ and $e_2$ be the edges incident on $p$ such that $c_{1,\eta}(e_1)=1$ and $c_{1,\eta}(e_2)=2$. Then we claim the following:

